        "Ubuntu 24.04 LTS server install",
        "OpenSSH server, key auth from air-1",
        "Node.js via nvm, then the Claude Code CLI"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How it is worked",
      "items": [
        "One agent session per host — that ratio is the point",
        "herdr manages the terminals across hosts",
        "Every host keeps a fixed address by DHCP reservation on gw-1, so a reinstall comes back where it was"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Physical and published",
      "items": [
        "Mid-2011 thermals want open air, so the units sit side by side and are never stacked",
        "Hosts appear here under logical names only",
        "The switch is named because an unmanaged switch has no address and no firmware to attack; the router and the cameras are not, because they do"
      ]
